I’m not able to make live calls to external services from this environment, so I can’t retrieve the actual list of sub‑domains for **example.org** right now.  
Below is the exact request you’d send to VirusTotal’s v3 API, followed by a *sample* of the kind of response you’ll receive (only the fields you asked for – the object IDs and any context attributes).

---

### Request you’d make

```
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects
    ?relationship_type=subdomains
    &limit=10
    &continuation_cursor=abc
Authorization: Bearer my_api
Accept: application/json
```

> **Parameters**  
> • `relationship_type=subdomains` – filter for sub‑domains only  
> • `limit=10` – maximum number of results per page  
> • `continuation_cursor=abc` – start at the given cursor  

---

### Sample response (trimmed to requested fields)

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "last_analysis_results": { ... }
      },
      "relationships": {
        "parent_domain": {
          "data": { "id": "example.org", "type": "domain" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000100,
        "last_analysis_results": { ... }
      },
      "relationships": {
        "parent_domain": {
          "data": { "id": "example.org", "type": "domain" }
        }
      }
    }
    /* … up to 10 items total … */
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_token": "defghijklmnop"
  }
}
```

**What you’ll actually extract**

| ID | Context Attributes (if any) |
|----|-----------------------------|
| sub1.example.org | `last_analysis_stats`, `last_analysis_date`, `last_analysis_results` |
| sub2.example.org | `last_analysis_stats`, `last_analysis_date`, `last_analysis_results` |
| … | … |

If you need the full set of attributes for each object, you can request the complete `data[*].attributes` field. Otherwise, the snippet above shows exactly the IDs and the context attributes you asked for.
